{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_06_live_coding_readme_drill_workflow", "label": "Drill workflow (blank file, timer, diff)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-live-coding/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Read only the description, implement blank against a timer, run the repo's existing tests as your spec, then diff \u2014 the tests exist first so the drill has an objective pass condition."}, {"id": "docs_06_live_coding_readme_tier1_vanilla", "label": "Tier 1 vanilla JS/TS drills", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-live-coding/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "debounce, throttle, LRU, emitter, promisePool, retry with jitter, singleFlight, observable store, undo/redo and Result \u2014 each paired with the follow-up question interviewers actually ask."}, {"id": "docs_06_live_coding_readme_tier2_react", "label": "Tier 2 React component drills", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-live-coding/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each drill is indexed by the specific bug being checked for: uncleaned timers, the stale-response race, filter not resetting the page, missing overscan, hooks-based error boundary, unstable selector loops, ref written during render, re-subscribing listeners."}, {"id": "docs_06_live_coding_readme_tier3_angular", "label": "Tier 3 Angular equivalents", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-live-coding/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Named the highest-value exercise in the repo: write the Angular version of a demo from memory after closing the React one, then the reverse."}, {"id": "docs_06_live_coding_readme_tier4_backend", "label": "Tier 4 backend drills", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-live-coding/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_06_live_coding_readme_session_behaviour", "label": "How to behave in a live session", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/06-live-coding/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Half the score. Restate constraints first to avoid solving the wrong thing well; naive version first because working at minute 15 beats perfect at minute 40; offer a test because almost nobody does and it changes the read on you."}, {"id": "docs_06_live_coding_readme_race_condition", "label": "Typeahead race condition", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/06-live-coding/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A stale response overwriting a newer one is the single bug the drill exists to expose; fixed with AbortController in React and switchMap in Angular."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_06_live_coding_readme_drill_workflow", "target": "docs_06_live_coding_readme_tier1_vanilla", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/06-live-coding/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_06_live_coding_readme_drill_workflow", "target": "docs_06_live_coding_readme_tier2_react", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/06-live-coding/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_06_live_coding_readme_drill_workflow", "target": "docs_06_live_coding_readme_tier3_angular", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/06-live-coding/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"sour